/*
 * Development Sample Data Seed Script
 * Description: Loads sample data for development environment
 * 
 * IDEMPOTENCY PATTERN (Reference Implementation):
 * ===============================================
 * This script demonstrates the ideal pattern for idempotent seed data scripts:
 * 
 * 1. TABLE-LEVEL IDEMPOTENCY:
 *    - Each table section checks if the table already has data
 *    - If data exists, the entire table section is skipped (performance optimization)
 *    - Uses: IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM table LIMIT 1)
 * 
 * 2. ROW-LEVEL IDEMPOTENCY:
 *    - Each INSERT statement uses ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING
 *    - Prevents duplicate key violations if script is run multiple times
 *    - Allows partial data loading (if some rows exist, only missing rows are inserted)
 *    - Uses: INSERT ... ON CONFLICT (primary_key) DO NOTHING
 * 
 * BENEFITS:
 * - Safe to run multiple times without errors
 * - Efficient: table-level check avoids unnecessary work
 * - Resilient: row-level check handles partial data scenarios
 * - Flexible: can add new rows without affecting existing data
 * 
 * USAGE:
 * - Run this script via DbUp on application startup
 * - Can be manually executed multiple times safely
 * - Works with Npgsql (no COPY FROM stdin required)
 * 
 * NOTE:
 * - Data is loaded in dependency order to respect foreign key constraints
 * - All INSERT statements use dollar-quoting ($qINSERT$) for safe multi-line strings
 */

-- Set search path to webshop schema
SET search_path TO webshop;

-- Disable statement timeout for large data loads
SET statement_timeout = 0;

DO $$
BEGIN
    RAISE NOTICE 'Starting seed data load process...';
    RAISE NOTICE 'Using idempotent pattern: table-level + row-level checks';
END $$;




